{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4062337","formula":"C₁₄H₇NaO₇S","hill":"C14H7NaO7S","elements":["H","C","O","Na","S"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":7.0,"O":7.0,"S":1.0,"Na":1.0},"names":{"en":"Sodium alizarinesulfonate","ru":"Ализариновый красный С"},"descriptions":{"en":"Alizarin Red S (also known as C.I. Mordant Red 3, Alizarin Carmine, and C.I 58005.) is a water-soluble sodium salt of Alizarin sulfonic acid with a chemical formula of C14H7NaO7S. Alizarin Red S was discovered by Graebe and Liebermann in 1871. In the field of histology alizarin Red S is used to stain calcium deposits in tissues, and in geology to stain and differentiate carbonate minerals.","ru":"Ализариновый красный С (ализарин С, alizarin red S, натриевая соль 9,10-дигидро-3,4-дигидрокси-9,10-диоксо-2-антраценсульфокислоты) — органическое соединение ряда антрахиноновых красителей с химической формулой C14H7NaO7S. Применяется в аналитической химии как индикатор для определения ионов алюминия, скандия, иттрия и фтора."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":3955344,"mass":342.26,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C2C(=C1)C(=O)C3=CC(=C(C(=C3C2=O)O)O)S(=O)(=O)[O-].[Na+]","inchikey":"HFVAFDPGUJEFBQ-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"sodium 3,4-dihydroxy-9,10-dioxoanthracene-2-sulfonate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"3955344","atoms":30,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.674,"y":1.266,"z":-0.163,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.867,"y":-0.113,"z":-0.093,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.767,"y":-0.969,"z":-0.026,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.467,"y":-0.445,"z":-0.029,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.273,"y":0.931,"z":-0.099,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.38,"y":1.789,"z":-0.166,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.91,"y":1.493,"z":-0.103,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.758,"y":2.707,"z":-0.165,"el":"O"},{"x":0.249,"y":0.577,"z":-0.031,"el":"C"},{"x":1.541,"y":1.107,"z":-0.034,"el":"C"},{"x":2.646,"y":0